BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20260817-infra-a5-flag-001-role-gating-off-the-client-writable-cookie-t
 3-su@healthclouda.com
DTSTAMP:20260810T120000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:[INFRA] A5/FLAG-001 - role gating off the client-writable cookie + 
 T3 suite
DESCRIPTION:The one security defect rather than hygiene item. hc_user is ht
 tpOnly:false (auth.ts:30) so the UI can read name/role - but every role ga
 te reads it too ([slug]/doctor/page.tsx:11 plus five siblings\, middleware
 .ts:68). A user can edit document.cookie and reach another org's dashboard
  shell.\n\nImpact today is limited: every real fetch carries the bearer to
 ken and DRF enforces server-side\, so they land in an empty skeleton getti
 ng 403s. VERIFY THAT ASSUMPTION rather than trusting it - nurse token agai
 nst a doctor-only endpoint should 403. If it ever doesn't\, this stops bei
 ng cosmetic.\n\nDone when: gating decides from a server-trusted source\, h
 c_user is display-only\, and T3 proves a tampered cookie renders nothing.\
 n\nDefault owner: @Bastoh (infra lane). Lane labels are ownership DEFAULTS
 \, not walls - either dev may take any item\, but claim its In Flight row 
 in HANDOFF.md before cutting the branch.\n\nPlan: docs/FRONTEND_SPRINT_PLA
 N.md
CATEGORIES:INFRA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
