DESCRIPTION:T3: tampered hc_user cookie against the DEPLOYMENT\, not just i
 n vitest. Every role\, every dashboard\, both cross-role and cross-org.\n\
 nT4 PHI leakage: patient IDs and HCL-IDs in URLs (they reach browser histo
 ry\, server logs and Referer headers) - browser cache and bfcache (press B
 ack after logout\, you must not see a dashboard) - what an error tracker w
 ould ship if we added one.\n\nT7 THE TIER TEST\, the one that matters most
 : trigger a REAL set-password email and a REAL consent link from the dev b
 ackend. Both must point at dev.healthclouda.com and complete end to end. F
 RONTEND_URL mistakes surface exactly here and nowhere earlier.\n\nAlso: no
  cookie carries Domain=.healthclouda.com\; the built output contains zero 
 occurrences of railway.app.\n\nBoth devs. Lane labels are ownership DEFAUL
 TS\, not walls - either dev may take any item\, but claim its In Flight ro
 w in HANDOFF.md before cutting the branch.\n\nPlan: docs/FRONTEND_SPRINT_P
 LAN.md
